      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above $a_{31}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}-2R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}-2R_{3}$.",
